@startuml
title The division trick: checking one value of the rule
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  DiamondBorderColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam ArrowColor #7A5BB5

start
:Storyteller claims: "my rule gives 10 at spot 3";
:Inspector builds a new list from the sealed notebook:
  new line = (old line - 10) / (spot - 3);
:Run the closeness check on the new list
(peek at a few lines, compute them on the fly);
if (Was the claim true?) then (yes)
  :New list follows a rule one step shorter
  (example: 4, 5, 7, 8 = spot + 3);<<#F3EEFB>>
  :Closeness check passes;
else (no)
  :New list is a mess
  (example: 4.5, 6, 6, 7.5);<<#FDEEEE>>
  :Closeness check fails;
endif
stop
@enduml
